# Functions Directory Requirements
#
# This file contains Python package dependencies for all functions in this directory.
# Packages listed here will be automatically installed when Open WebUI starts.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file to requirements.txt
#   2. Add your dependencies (one per line)
#   3. Restart Open WebUI - packages will be installed automatically
#
# Format:
#   package_name==version      # Pin to specific version (recommended)
#   package_name>=version      # Minimum version
#   package_name               # Latest version (not recommended for production)
#
# Examples:
#   requests==2.31.0
#   openai>=1.0.0
#   pandas==2.0.0
#   numpy>=1.24.0
#
# Common packages for Open WebUI functions:
#   - requests: HTTP requests
#   - openai: OpenAI API
#   - anthropic: Anthropic Claude API
#   - google-generativeai: Google Gemini API
#   - pydantic: Data validation
#   - aiohttp: Async HTTP
#   - beautifulsoup4: HTML parsing
#   - python-dateutil: Date utilities
#
# Note: Individual functions can also specify requirements in their frontmatter.
# Those will be installed in addition to packages listed here.
